      "problem": "$\\int (8+8{cot}^{2}⁡(4x+3))\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ with $\\theta =4x+3,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(4x+3)={csc}^{2}⁡(4x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (8+8{cot}^{2}⁡(4x+3))\\text{d}x & =8\\int (1+{cot}^{2}⁡(4x+3))\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int {csc}^{2}⁡(4x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8[-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x+3)]+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x+3)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
